>> title: Smoked Chicken
>> category: Smoked & Grilled
>> tags: chicken, poultry, barbecue, smoker, spatchcock
>> counters: Smokehouse, The Bowl Shop
>> aka: bbq chicken, barbeque chicken, smoked half chicken, pit chicken, half a chicken
>> servings: 4
>> time: 7 hr 45 min
>> slack: unforgiving — the temperature here is a safety number and not a preference: 165°F in the breast, 175°F in the thigh, never the clock
>> pairs-with: coleslaw

Bring the #smoker{} to 275°F (135°C) over cherry or hickory and hold it there.

>> step: butterfly, rub over and under the skin
Cut the backbone out of @whole chicken{4%lb}(1.8 kg) and press it flat, then rub it over and under the skin with @unsalted butter{2%Tbs}(28 g, softened), @kosher salt{1%Tbs}, @smoked paprika{2%tsp}, @garlic powder{1%tsp}, @onion powder{1%tsp}, and @coarse black pepper{1%tsp}.

>> step: chill uncovered 4 hr, to dry the skin
Leave @&(~1)seasoned chicken{} uncovered on a rack in the fridge to ~chill{4%hr}, which is what dries the skin enough to crisp at this heat.

>> step: smoke 275°F (135°C) 3 hr, to 165°F (74°C)
Smoke @&(~1)chicken{} skin side up for ~smoke{3%hr}, to 165°F (74°C) in the thickest of the breast and 175°F (79°C) in the thigh.

>> step: stir a glaze
Stir @barbecue sauce{1/3%cup}(80 mL) with @cider vinegar{1%Tbs} until it brushes on thin.

>> step: brush, set 15 min, rest 15 min, cut into eight
Brush @&(~1)glaze{} over @&(~2)smoked chicken{} and return it to the smoker until the glaze sets, ~smoke{15%min}, then ~rest{15%min} and cut it into eight.
